WEBVTT

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:04.000
We can definitely live together amicably

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:14.000
Do it more gently.

00:02:15.370 --> 00:02:16.290
Like that...

00:02:19.460 --> 00:02:21.290
How is it? Are you okay?

00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:23.980
It's just because I slept in a weird position.

00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:28.720
So you say, but it doesn't mean
you get to skip out on water carrying duty.

00:02:28.910 --> 00:02:30.130
I'm not trying...

00:02:32.210 --> 00:02:33.730
You shouldn't push yourself too hard.

00:02:34.030 --> 00:02:35.730
I'll switch duties with you.

00:02:36.070 --> 00:02:37.830
Thanks. Sorry.

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:39.730
Nicely done.

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:41.000
Shingo!

00:02:42.050 --> 00:02:43.510
But, Howard...

00:02:44.020 --> 00:02:47.210
There's no use fighting over something like water carrying.

00:02:48.820 --> 00:02:51.860
I wish I had a sore neck from sleeping at a bad angle too.

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:53.380
Howard, stop it!

00:02:54.220 --> 00:02:55.040
You should talk!

00:02:55.510 --> 00:02:58.630
You're the one who always gets
Bell to do his water-carrying for him.

00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:01.340
I'm better suited to hunting.

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:05.040
Despite which you still haven't caught a single thing.

00:03:05.490 --> 00:03:09.330
Are you sure you're not taking
a nap when you say you're going hunting?

00:03:09.330 --> 00:03:10.570
What did you say?

00:03:10.570 --> 00:03:12.970
If you're frustrated, catch something
for once and prove me wrong.

00:03:12.970 --> 00:03:14.210
Now you've said it!

00:03:14.530 --> 00:03:16.890
Stop it!

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:21.280
Both of you, give it a break!

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:23.470
You bicker from dawn until dusk!

00:03:23.860 --> 00:03:24.820
Sharla...

00:03:25.230 --> 00:03:29.000
Why can't you get along? There's nobody here but us!

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:31.720
And yet, every day you do nothing but argue!

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:34.870
I'm sick of it! Sick to death!

00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:38.470
Now she's cryin'.

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:41.390
It's okay. It's okay, Sharla.

00:03:42.350 --> 00:03:44.110
But it's just like Sharla said.

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:46.340
What's wrong with you two?

00:03:46.890 --> 00:03:48.710
Lately you've been strangely irritated.

00:03:49.030 --> 00:03:50.380
Because Howard...

00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:51.650
It's you!

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:53.190
See, again!

00:03:54.130 --> 00:03:55.290
They're not to blame.

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:57.650
It's only natural that they'd be so irritated.

00:03:58.530 --> 00:04:00.500
And there's a reason for it.

00:04:01.630 --> 00:04:04.100
Because of everyone's hard work,
we have a water supply.

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:06.520
We've also have a map of where to get food.

00:04:07.420 --> 00:04:13.230
But if you think about it, in  this heat, we spend most of the day gathering food and carrying water.

00:04:13.890 --> 00:04:17.240
At night, we can't sleep restfully in the shuttle's seats.

00:04:18.460 --> 00:04:20.260
Exhaustion is building in everyone.

00:04:20.830 --> 00:04:26.960
That's true, but we hafta collect food,
'n there's nowhere to sleep but the shuttle.

00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:34.120
We'll just have to move.

00:04:36.520 --> 00:04:37.740
To Fairy Lake!

00:04:38.540 --> 00:04:39.970
Fairy Lake?

00:04:39.970 --> 00:04:44.020
There's lots of fruit and water there,
and there's even fish.

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:48.820
Gathering food will be easy,
and it'd be cooler because we'd be in the forest.

00:04:49.310 --> 00:04:51.090
I think we'd have much easier living.

00:04:51.820 --> 00:04:54.710
But that big monster is there.

00:04:55.230 --> 00:04:57.140
There was the giant lizard, too.

00:04:57.560 --> 00:04:59.080
But there's The Great Tree.

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:02.920
Didn't Shingo say it?

00:05:03.260 --> 00:05:05.880
"Wouldn't it be great if we could build a house up there?"

00:05:07.230 --> 00:05:09.200
That was just an idea.

00:05:10.630 --> 00:05:14.040
Hey, that giant lizard definitely
can't get to the top of that tree.

00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:16.630
Don't say it like it's so simple!

00:05:16.940 --> 00:05:17.880
Why not?

00:05:18.740 --> 00:05:22.910
If eight people're gonna live in a house, it needs to be strong 'n spacious enough for everyone.

00:05:23.210 --> 00:05:27.650
We won't know if we can build
a house in a tree that size 'til we investigate it.

00:05:27.890 --> 00:05:29.530
That's true, but...

00:05:29.940 --> 00:05:32.080
But I think there's merit in looking into it.

00:05:32.690 --> 00:05:34.330
How about it? Shall we go see?

00:05:35.110 --> 00:05:36.130
Why not?

00:05:37.030 --> 00:05:38.210
Everyone else?

00:05:43.190 --> 00:05:44.230
Then it's decided.

00:05:44.640 --> 00:05:46.660
After we've eaten breakfast we'll set out.

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:53.530
Kaoru, take care of things here, okay?

00:05:54.010 --> 00:05:55.790
We'll be back by evening.

00:06:24.580 --> 00:06:27.440
It'll work, it'll work! It won't collapse either!

00:06:27.690 --> 00:06:29.380
Check the other branches too, please!

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:31.310
Chako, please.

00:06:43.780 --> 00:06:45.010
How is it?

00:06:46.550 --> 00:06:49.830
The tree's density, number of rings,
and the spread of the roots...

00:06:50.690 --> 00:06:52.120
...are all just fine.

00:06:52.570 --> 00:06:55.310
It'll hold up the weight of a house with more to spare.

00:06:55.760 --> 00:06:56.580
Really?

00:06:57.370 --> 00:06:59.260
If you made it above there...

00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:02.340
...we'll be protected from that big thing
that attacked the shuttle, am I right?

00:07:10.270 --> 00:07:11.190
That's true...

00:07:11.430 --> 00:07:13.290
It doesn't seem like he can climb trees.

00:07:14.710 --> 00:07:16.340
We'll be fine up there!

00:07:20.450 --> 00:07:22.850
All of a sudden I'm really motivated!

00:07:23.410 --> 00:07:26.580
Hey, let's look into the size of
the tree and stuff in more detail.

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:29.510
We still hafta make the blueprints.

00:07:29.960 --> 00:07:30.710
Okay!

00:07:31.460 --> 00:07:32.710
Howard!

00:07:32.940 --> 00:07:36.200
We're going to collect some water and food!

00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:38.200
No helping that.

00:08:07.400 --> 00:08:09.160
It's 9.6 metres.

00:08:09.370 --> 00:08:11.490
9.6 metres...

00:08:11.940 --> 00:08:13.680
Next is the left end.

00:08:13.960 --> 00:08:15.650
That's the right from your side, Shingo.

00:08:16.230 --> 00:08:17.240
Okay!

00:08:18.520 --> 00:08:19.760
Is around here okay?

00:08:19.850 --> 00:08:20.880
Perfect!

00:08:29.240 --> 00:08:31.290
Sharla, you look somehow happy.

00:08:33.160 --> 00:08:36.220
I feel like if we live here,
we can definitely live together amicably.

00:08:37.550 --> 00:08:38.490
Me too.

00:08:55.660 --> 00:08:58.120
They're acting like it's so much fun.

00:09:08.690 --> 00:09:09.880
Kaoru!

00:09:10.510 --> 00:09:11.660
Hey!

00:09:17.810 --> 00:09:19.210
So, shall we start?

00:09:20.020 --> 00:09:21.540
Shingo, Chako, please.

00:09:21.860 --> 00:09:22.530
Okay.

00:09:22.960 --> 00:09:24.030
Ta-da!

00:09:24.280 --> 00:09:26.530
This is our survey map of The Great Tree.

00:09:27.430 --> 00:09:29.790
Did you guys really make that?

00:09:30.760 --> 00:09:31.940
Of course we did!

00:09:32.240 --> 00:09:33.710
It's a piece of cake!

00:09:35.210 --> 00:09:37.030
You're useful once in a while.

00:09:38.110 --> 00:09:39.840
What'd you say?

00:09:40.380 --> 00:09:41.190
Chako!

00:09:41.430 --> 00:09:43.250
And? Shingo, how is it?

00:09:43.760 --> 00:09:46.780
Our conclusion is that there's
no problem with the strength.

00:09:47.510 --> 00:09:50.660
The trunk bends to support the foundation.

00:09:51.160 --> 00:09:53.110
I think we can build a comfortable house.

00:09:54.240 --> 00:09:55.630
Then it's decided!

00:09:56.090 --> 00:09:59.130
Now I can finally stretch out my body and sleep!

00:10:00.220 --> 00:10:01.380
Isn't it great?

00:10:04.700 --> 00:10:06.610
Alright! My room will be here.

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:08.790
With a view of Fairy Lake.

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:11.600
Idiot! You think you're gettin' a room?

00:10:11.600 --> 00:10:12.690
Why not?

00:10:13.630 --> 00:10:16.010
Why not? There's no space for it!

00:10:16.480 --> 00:10:18.030
There should be enough for it.

00:10:18.290 --> 00:10:19.210
No way, no way!

00:10:19.380 --> 00:10:20.560
I'm opposed to it.

00:10:21.540 --> 00:10:23.980
I know that it's physically possible to build a house.

00:10:24.730 --> 00:10:27.390
And the giant lizard can't reach that high.

00:10:27.930 --> 00:10:30.630
...but, I think the shuttle is definitely safer.

00:10:31.100 --> 00:10:34.780
Practically speaking, it did protect us
from the sea snake and that giant monster.

00:10:35.410 --> 00:10:38.360
And we have yet to investigate this entire island.

00:10:39.310 --> 00:10:41.680
There's a possibility that even larger creatures exist.

00:10:42.030 --> 00:10:44.490
That may be true, but...

00:10:46.490 --> 00:10:50.130
I say, don't worry about it.
I'll beat up anything like that.

00:10:50.490 --> 00:10:51.430
Can you?

00:10:52.060 --> 00:10:53.470
Can you beat them up?

00:10:53.980 --> 00:10:54.970
That is...

00:10:54.970 --> 00:10:56.580
Everyone's lives are depending on it.

00:10:56.920 --> 00:10:58.290
Don't say something so irresponsible!

00:10:58.870 --> 00:11:01.250
Then why don't you stay behind on your own?

00:11:01.570 --> 00:11:03.460
Whatever anyone says, I'm going.

00:11:03.950 --> 00:11:06.410
It'll be much better than that cramped shuttle.

00:11:08.730 --> 00:11:09.890
What should we do?

00:11:16.590 --> 00:11:17.730
...acting so important...

00:11:18.840 --> 00:11:21.410
There's certainly an advantage to Menori's suggestion.

00:11:21.580 --> 00:11:24.240
But the stress of living in the shuttle is too great.

00:11:24.800 --> 00:11:27.580
I think in the end it would be best
if we moved to Fairy Lake.

00:11:28.340 --> 00:11:32.130
If it seems we're in danger,
we can still return to the shuttle.

00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:34.180
I simply spoke my objection.

00:11:34.830 --> 00:11:37.270
The decision, Luna, is yours to make as the leader.

00:11:48.710 --> 00:11:49.550
I've decided.

00:11:50.860 --> 00:11:54.690
We'll build a house and move to Fairy Lake.

00:11:54.690 --> 00:11:57.330
Alright! That's how it should be!

00:12:08.960 --> 00:12:10.120
It's a saw.

00:12:10.530 --> 00:12:13.190
I see! You cut that firewood with that, right?

00:12:13.630 --> 00:12:15.540
You'll need it to build the house.

00:12:16.340 --> 00:12:17.240
Kaoru!

00:12:17.430 --> 00:12:19.760
Shingo! We can't fall behind!

00:12:20.170 --> 00:12:22.910
We'll stay up all night 'n draw up
the blueprints for the house!

00:12:32.490 --> 00:12:34.420
Windows at east and west, right?

00:12:34.850 --> 00:12:37.760
The window facing the lake should be big!

00:12:37.940 --> 00:12:39.560
The door'll be on the south side.

00:12:40.530 --> 00:12:41.960
The north will be the back.

00:12:42.520 --> 00:12:46.250
The bad spot next to the house on
the north is Howard's room.

00:12:47.860 --> 00:12:49.480
We're really going to make that?

00:12:49.490 --> 00:12:52.910
He'll just be confused that we actually did it, so why not?

00:12:53.060 --> 00:12:54.520
That might be worth it.

00:12:57.730 --> 00:12:58.890
By the way, how's your neck?

00:13:00.460 --> 00:13:02.110
Now that you mention it, I guess it's better!

00:13:02.540 --> 00:13:05.540
That's great! Anyways, let's finish up here quick!

00:13:05.750 --> 00:13:06.390
Yeah!

00:13:06.390 --> 00:13:07.290
Alright!

00:13:32.490 --> 00:13:33.760
Everyone, we're finished.

00:13:34.930 --> 00:13:36.460
This is our house.

00:13:38.660 --> 00:13:40.980
And over there, it's drawn in actual size.

00:13:42.070 --> 00:13:43.930
This is our house!

00:13:44.090 --> 00:13:45.410
It looks like it will be very nice.

00:13:46.980 --> 00:13:49.250
My room is in a place like this.

00:13:49.640 --> 00:13:52.660
I think you should be thankful that
we actually gave you your own room.

00:13:52.960 --> 00:13:55.760
It was hard to make space for it.

00:13:56.260 --> 00:13:57.760
What, d'you think we shoulda done without?

00:14:03.690 --> 00:14:07.490
Since we have our blueprints finished,
we'll start making it today.

00:14:08.170 --> 00:14:11.430
It'll involve a lot of hard labour, but let's all do our best.

00:14:14.640 --> 00:14:16.510
Today I'll stay behind here.

00:14:17.190 --> 00:14:19.180
What, tryin' to slack off again?

00:14:19.930 --> 00:14:21.220
The fire watch!

00:14:21.880 --> 00:14:24.840
And also fishing for the sake of
everyone who'll be coming home tired!

00:14:25.460 --> 00:14:26.360
Yeah, yeah.

00:14:26.690 --> 00:14:27.890
I mean it!

00:14:28.230 --> 00:14:30.130
Well then, we'll be expecting it.

00:14:30.500 --> 00:14:32.000
We'll be back by tonight.

00:14:33.430 --> 00:14:34.700
Have fun at work!

00:14:40.640 --> 00:14:41.830
Good luck!

00:14:47.880 --> 00:14:50.170
So let's start by building the foundation.

00:14:50.390 --> 00:14:53.340
This is an important part,
so look for trees very carefully.

00:14:53.860 --> 00:14:55.100
The width should be this much.

00:14:55.340 --> 00:14:57.800
And as hard and straight as possible.

00:14:58.190 --> 00:15:00.500
When you find one, Chako will check it out.

00:15:00.800 --> 00:15:02.580
Got it. Well, let's start!

00:15:02.580 --> 00:15:03.560
--Sure.     --Yeah.
--Let's go.

00:15:06.860 --> 00:15:08.640
How is it? Is it a good tree?

00:15:08.640 --> 00:15:09.430
Let's see...

00:15:15.370 --> 00:15:17.110
No good, bugs are eating it.

00:15:17.320 --> 00:15:19.420
I thought it was such a good tree, too.

00:15:19.910 --> 00:15:22.180
Well, no choice but to look for another.

00:15:22.180 --> 00:15:23.410
Chako!

00:15:23.530 --> 00:15:25.120
I'll just check over there.

00:15:26.190 --> 00:15:28.360
How about we search over there next?

00:15:31.480 --> 00:15:33.780
Perfect. We can use this.

00:15:34.140 --> 00:15:34.930
Bell...

00:15:36.140 --> 00:15:38.360
Cut it at around this height.

00:15:38.840 --> 00:15:39.820
Got it.

00:15:52.490 --> 00:15:55.810
Oh, they're here. They even come to such a shallow place.

00:15:57.260 --> 00:15:59.690
It seems like I could catch a hundred in no time.

00:16:02.790 --> 00:16:03.560
How is it?

00:16:04.740 --> 00:16:05.730
This one's okay.

00:16:11.680 --> 00:16:12.580
Stand back!

00:16:58.140 --> 00:17:01.340
I didn't think cutting down trees would be this hard.

00:17:01.630 --> 00:17:04.270
'N we only have part of the foundation.

00:17:04.930 --> 00:17:07.610
If we don't finish the foundation,
we can't move on to the next step.

00:17:08.190 --> 00:17:09.800
In the mean time, let's try putting them together.

00:17:28.630 --> 00:17:29.980
Well, let's start!

00:17:30.590 --> 00:17:32.640
Pull slowly so you don't hurt your shoulders.

00:17:33.290 --> 00:17:33.930
Start!

00:17:46.080 --> 00:17:47.110
It rose.

00:17:47.430 --> 00:17:48.760
It really rose!

00:17:48.760 --> 00:17:50.600
Still good... still good...

00:17:54.630 --> 00:17:55.780
Kaoru, stop!

00:18:06.050 --> 00:18:07.360
Pull slowly.

00:18:12.950 --> 00:18:14.340
Alright, here it comes...

00:18:14.560 --> 00:18:15.580
Just like that.

00:18:17.450 --> 00:18:18.010
Watch out!

00:18:25.360 --> 00:18:27.030
Is anyone hurt?

00:18:27.390 --> 00:18:28.440
We're all fine.

00:18:29.260 --> 00:18:30.460
Kaoru! How's your hand?

00:18:31.120 --> 00:18:31.980
It's fine.

00:18:33.070 --> 00:18:34.290
Then one more time.

00:18:43.440 --> 00:18:44.260
It's here, it's here.

00:18:44.260 --> 00:18:45.460
Alright, that's good.

00:18:49.510 --> 00:18:51.840
Bell, Kaoru, give us slack a little at a time.

00:19:00.710 --> 00:19:01.440
We did it!

00:19:01.440 --> 00:19:02.640
It's perfect.

00:19:10.780 --> 00:19:12.140
It seems okay.

00:19:12.330 --> 00:19:14.490
That's great! Okay, the next one!

00:19:21.280 --> 00:19:22.490
I can't fish.

00:19:23.710 --> 00:19:24.990
I'll just give up.

00:19:41.170 --> 00:19:42.820
With this, the foundation is finished.

00:19:45.310 --> 00:19:46.190
Wow!

00:19:46.550 --> 00:19:49.960
We can really make our own house.

00:19:50.280 --> 00:19:52.080
Oh, it's really coming along!

00:19:52.810 --> 00:19:54.780
Although I guess it's still just the foundation.

00:19:55.250 --> 00:19:57.070
I just came to see how it was going.

00:19:57.440 --> 00:20:01.100
So you say, but I bet you couldn't catch a thing.

00:20:02.430 --> 00:20:03.690
What are you saying?

00:20:04.010 --> 00:20:07.030
I was just worried that everyone was in trouble.

00:20:07.510 --> 00:20:09.780
And what happened to the fire watch?

00:20:10.100 --> 00:20:11.490
It's just fine.

00:20:11.900 --> 00:20:14.470
No, we don't know if somethin's happened.

00:20:15.030 --> 00:20:17.320
What do you plan to do
if it's started a forest fire?

00:20:19.720 --> 00:20:22.030
I think that's enough, Chako.

00:20:22.290 --> 00:20:24.230
I mean, Howard doesn't think about anyone but himself...

00:20:24.340 --> 00:20:24.910
Yeah, yeah.

00:20:24.920 --> 00:20:29.390
Under these circumstances
you can't let every little thing get to you.

00:20:31.400 --> 00:20:32.880
So this is my room.

00:20:42.030 --> 00:20:44.040
It's got a pretty good view.

00:20:44.540 --> 00:20:47.380
But it's still just the frame that's done.

00:20:51.480 --> 00:20:53.060
Stop it, Howard!

00:20:53.410 --> 00:20:55.720
What? I'm just checking it out.

00:20:57.890 --> 00:20:59.410
Stop, Howard!

00:20:59.680 --> 00:21:01.420
It's fine, it's fine!

00:21:17.430 --> 00:21:18.800
I'm saved.

00:21:23.360 --> 00:21:24.780
What did you think you were doing?

00:21:25.720 --> 00:21:28.590
We worked so hard to make it... Couldn't you tell?!

00:21:29.860 --> 00:21:32.980
What were you thinking, jumping up
and down on it so enthusiastically?

00:21:33.390 --> 00:21:35.540
You don't have to get so mad!

00:21:35.690 --> 00:21:37.310
It's not like I did it on purpose!

00:21:37.310 --> 00:21:38.690
It's obvious!

00:21:38.690 --> 00:21:41.150
You don't help, and only do what you want!

00:21:42.310 --> 00:21:44.130
Howard, you don't know...

00:21:44.340 --> 00:21:46.550
...how much trouble we went through.

00:21:46.680 --> 00:21:47.830
And what about it?

00:21:48.240 --> 00:21:50.810
However much work it was, we can't live in this!

00:21:52.040 --> 00:21:53.110
Well I'm right, aren't I?

00:21:53.430 --> 00:21:55.960
It broke just from me putting my weight on it.

00:21:56.360 --> 00:21:58.140
Eight people couldn't live in that!

00:21:58.890 --> 00:22:01.210
The best we could hope for is that
it would collapse as soon as we moved in.

00:22:01.660 --> 00:22:03.030
This wasn't a house.

00:22:03.950 --> 00:22:06.090
It's a good thing it broke so soon!

00:22:06.090 --> 00:22:07.230
Now you've said it!

00:22:07.910 --> 00:22:08.730
Stop it!

00:22:10.010 --> 00:22:11.580
I understand how you feel, Shingo...

00:22:12.180 --> 00:22:13.490
...since we all worked so hard...

00:22:14.210 --> 00:22:14.790
...but...

00:22:15.520 --> 00:22:17.660
...it couldn't hold up one person's weight.

00:22:18.290 --> 00:22:20.640
It was too weak for eight people to live in it.

00:22:22.480 --> 00:22:24.890
It seems we have no choice but to live in the shuttle.

00:22:50.430 --> 00:22:52.270
The shuttle's broken!

00:22:52.510 --> 00:22:53.980
The fire's gone out too!

00:22:54.430 --> 00:22:55.830
What happened here?

00:23:04.380 --> 00:23:08.390
Who did it? Who smashed up our
precious shuttle like that?

00:23:08.750 --> 00:23:11.660
But this is no time to get downtrodden.

00:23:11.840 --> 00:23:15.130
We have to think seriously
about moving to The Great Tree.

00:23:15.880 --> 00:23:16.590
That's true.

00:23:16.960 --> 00:23:20.360
And anyways, there's lots of
useful-lookin' things in the shuttle.

00:23:20.860 --> 00:23:23.490
Now that we're decided,
there's nothing to do but go forward!

00:23:23.620 --> 00:23:24.390
Yeah!

00:23:25.400 --> 00:23:27.590
Next time: Let's build a house.
